  "sampleAnswer": "Equivalence Partitioning divides inputs into groups expected to behave similarly, allowing representative values to reduce redundant tests. For an age field accepting 18–60, useful partitions include below 18, 18–60, and above 60, with invalid-format partitions as appropriate.",
